OL,3,GNEWSAGeorge thought his funeral was
OL,4,Apaid for ` but now his wife will get
OL,5,Anothing when he dies
OL,6,
OL,7,FFor 17 years, George Davies made
OL,8,Fpayments to an insurance company to
OL,9,Fcover the cost of his funeral.
OL,11,FThe 82-year-old, who has stage 4
OL,12,Fcancer, thought he had prepared and
OL,13,Fprovided for his wife Marion.
OL,15,FBut now he isn't entitled to a penny.
OL,17,FGeorge took the policy out through his
OL,18,Flocal credit union, but it was
OL,19,Fcancelled after the company backing the
OL,20,Fproduct pulled out of the UK.
